= Corpus evidence =

This page records the first empirical corpus test of the [[BITwiki:V1 to V2 maturation|V1 → V2 maturation]] architecture.

The governing question is not “What ontology can we imagine?” It is:

<blockquote>'''What distinctions does the actual corpus require us to represent?'''</blockquote>

The machine-readable evidence is generated by <code>scripts/inventory_corpus.py</code> during pull-request validation. The workflow emits:

* <code>v2-corpus-inventory.json</code> — every deployable V2 MediaWiki page, its namespace/title, redirect state, categories, explicit Knowledge object fields, source status, and source-syntax semantic annotations;
* <code>v1-classification-usage.json</code> — every one of the 162 archived V1 Main pages with API-recorded categories/templates, revision identity, subpage status, Infobox type source parameter, classification source syntax, and Topic signal;
* <code>v2-validation.json</code> — structural V2 validation.

These outputs are evidence artifacts, not a substitute for human interpretation.

== V2 Main-namespace reality ==

At the first complete inventory pass, the V2 Main namespace contains '''49 pages''':

{| class="wikitable"
! Role !! Count
|-
| V1 compatibility or other redirects || 36
|-
| Explicit <code>Knowledge object</code> pages || 12
|-
| Main Page || 1
|-
| Other non-redirect Main pages || 0
|}

This is the most important finding of the first corpus pass.

'''V2 is currently a strong architectural and semantic scaffold, but its canonical subject corpus is still deliberately small.'''

The twelve explicit knowledge objects are the twelve domain exemplars. Their current explicit identity distribution is:

* Entity type: <code>Concept</code> — 12 / 12;
* Epistemic status: <code>Established</code> — 12 / 12;
* Domain: one exemplar in each current domain — Systems science, Science, Biology, Mathematics, Philosophy, Technology, Electronics, Energy, Engineering, Chemistry, Physics, and Medicine.

There are no current Main-namespace non-redirect knowledge pages outside that exemplar set, and no explicit V2 classification reuse of the historical <code>Topic</code> or <code>Idea</code> values.

=== What this does not prove ===

It does '''not''' prove that every future BITwiki object is a Concept.

It proves only that the current intentionally small exemplar corpus exercises the Concept path. The present V2 corpus therefore cannot yet empirically validate or invalidate the rest of the base Entity type vocabulary.

Adding or deleting types from this evidence alone would be circular: the corpus has not yet been migrated deeply enough to test them.

== V1 Main-namespace reality ==

The archived V1 Main namespace contains '''162 pages'''. The complete page-level inventory finds:

{| class="wikitable"
! Signal !! Count
|-
| Main pages inventoried || 162
|-
| Subpages || 14
|-
| Pages with any classification / Topic signal || 130
|-
| Pages without classification / Topic signal || 32
|-
| Pages with classification-property source syntax || 83
|-
| Pages with an API-recorded identity-like category || 85
|-
| Pages carrying an Infobox <code>type</code> source parameter || 78
|-
| Pages containing the literal term <code>Topic</code> || 48
|}

The absence of classification on 32 pages is itself evidence. It is concentrated partly in:

* Book-Matter-like subpages such as the Bioluminescent Organisms and Fluorescent Coral Reefs section families;
* epistemic subpages;
* Main Page sections;
* component/section fragments;
* maintenance/test pages;
* miscellaneous historical interface or organizational material.

Therefore “page has no entity type” must not automatically be interpreted as “V2 needs another entity type.” Some pages are not first-class knowledge objects at all.

