These are '''implementation evidence''' because the memberships were returned by MediaWiki and preserved in <code>archive-v1/index.json</code>.

They are not proof that Category was the correct semantic primitive. V1 used categories for several jobs simultaneously, and [[BITwiki:V1 category migration]] already establishes that category membership must be interpreted functionally before migration.

The dominance of <code>Concepts</code> is especially important: it shows how much V1 content was collapsed into a broad category even while the design documents articulated richer type distinctions.

